WEBVTT

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.480
Oh, the latest paper here.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.740
You want a hot iron of a Hunziker's collar?

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.620
Two rolls got fresh with the baker.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.520
Hey, the late paper just came in.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.660
Who wants the late paper?

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.970
minute, Mr. Weldon. I think...

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.080
I'm sorry. I thought I heard Mr. Falco.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.510
Yes, I'll tell him when he returns.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:29.970
I know he's been...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.940
I've been trying to get in touch with him the third time he's called today.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.040
He probably wants me to break a leg.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.580
No, an army said.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.940
I told him you were sure the item would be in Mr. Hunsaker's column in tomorrow's paper.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:44.480
It isn't.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:50.090
I saw the early edition.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.540
But Sidney...

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.760
But, but, but, but, but what?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.760
That makes five days in a row Mr. Hunsaker's cut you out of his column.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.360
May I rent you out as an adding machine?

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.130
Get me Joe Robard. Anybody else call?

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.620
The renting agent and your tailor.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.210
Pay the rent and tell the tailor to wait.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.600
Leave much balance in the bank.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:17.660
Hello, Mr. Robard? Could you locate him, please?

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:28.440
Here. Let me run a 50-yard dash with my legs cut off.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:29.390
Hey, Joe!

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.160
Joe, it's Sidney. How do you like this? I'm running out of alibis.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.670
Oh, no, no, no. I asked J.J. to withhold the item until he gave you a fine, fat paragraph.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.330
You're a liar, Sidney.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:40.440
Liar.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.560
Oh, it's a publicity man's nature to be a liar. I wouldn't hire you if you wasn't a liar.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:50.800
I'd pay you a C and a half where you plant big lies about me and the club all over the map.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:57.050
Yeah, I mean in that sense, but also in the sense that you are a person a liar, too,

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.150
because you don't do the work that I pay you for.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:04:59.960
Wait a minute.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.300
Wait a minute, Joe. When I spoke to J.J. last night, he said...

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.780
Wish I could help in some way, Sidney.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.620
You could help with two minutes of silence.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.970
I hate to see you like this, Sidney.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.140
if you feel nervous.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.780
So what will you do if I feel nervous?

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.880
Open your meaty, sympathetic arms.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.090
Oh, Sidney, you got me so I don't know what to do.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.900
Well, you ought to know me by now.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:54.930
I know you.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.250
No, no, you don't.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:05.430
Well, I'm no hero. I'm nice to people where it pays me to be nice.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:08.490
Look, I do it enough on the outside, so don't expect me to do it in my own office.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.330
I'll bind right now with Hunsaker.

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:17.130
Sidney, maybe I'm done, but why does Mr. Hunsaker want to squeeze your livelihood away?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.340
What do you stand for that kind of treatment for?

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:25.440
He's punishing me. His kid sister's having a romance with some guitar player.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.700
He asked me to break it up. I thought I did, but maybe I didn't.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:29.970
Now I've got to go find him.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.620
And Hunsick is the golden ladder to the places I want to get.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.500
Sidney, you make a living. Where do you want to get?

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.490
We up high, Sam, where it's always balmy.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:42.600
And no one snaps his fingers and says,

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:43.840
Hey, shrimp, rack the balls.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.040
Or, hey, Mouse, Mouse, go out and buy me a pack of butts.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.180
I don't want tips from the kitty. I'm in the big game with the big players.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:54.500
My experience I can give you in a nutshell, and I didn't dream it in a dream either.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:59.970
Dog eat dog. In brief, from now on, the best of everything is good enough for me.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.950
Sidney, I'm not trying to tell you what to do.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.760
It's just that it makes me feel bad when Mr. Hunsaker hurts you.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.060
Every dog will have his day.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:11.740
That's for me. Tear it up.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:18.480
Sidney, Falco office. Take your top coat.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.380
And leave a tip in every hatchet room in town.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:23.090
One, two, three, four.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.200
Did she get Nessage's eyelashes?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:49.400
I called you twice.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:50.880
Hey, man, I've been up to here.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.920
Look, Susie Hunsaker, JJ's sister.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.320
She been in, I mean lately, in the last couple of days.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:00.800
I don't think so.

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:01.380
Are you sure?

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:02.500
Find out for me.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:03.760
Sidney?

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.150
Sidney, can I talk to you a minute?

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:07.800
Have you seen Frank D'Angelo around?

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:08.800
At the bar.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:11.560
Sidney, I'm in trouble.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:21.900
Give my nephew a drink.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.420
Your nephew doesn't want a drink.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.800
That's a lollipop, that boy.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:26.860
The kid's only great.

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:29.860
10% of his future, you're great too.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:36.860
Frank, I think maybe you lied to me.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:44.100
Look, Sidney, you're my own sister's son,

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:46.520
but where does that give you the right to call me a liar?

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.650
I thought you said that your boy was washed up with Susie Hunsaker.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.950
Yeah, and it's the truth, to the best of my knowledge.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.710
Frankly, I'm glad, for Steve's sake, not yours.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:59.670
I handle these boys with their best interests at heart.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.100
Steve shouldn't get mixed up with no bimbo at his age.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.060
Listen, Frank, you better be telling me the truth.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.920
I don't like this threatening attitude.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.560
I told you what I know, now go make yourself a holiday.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.980
Come to think of it, what business of yours, what they do, this boy and girl?

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:28.230
If you knew Hunsaker as well as I did, you might understand why it is my business.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:29.890
You're walking around.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:34.670
blind Frank without a cane and in case you didn't know it Susie Hunsick is out

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:48.930
in the back right now thank you very much on behalf of the quintet Chico

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:51.790
Paul Hamilton, Fred Katz, Paul Horne, Carson Smith, and myself.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.840
While we're away, the Elysian Room is...

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:54.100
Hey, Chief.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.780
Hey, Paul, call this chick here when I go get Steve.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.880
An interesting fusion of the tradition.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.560
I just wanted to ask you how you came to form the group.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.620
Well, we just sort of got together.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.720
Look, why don't you ask Fred Katz? He writes all this stuff.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:13.120
Mr. Katz, I'm very interested in jazz.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:22.540
Nancy Hanson.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:35.080
Steve, try to make you a good wife.

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:45.390
Where's the cat?

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:46.760
Who?

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:48.330
Is he around?

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:50.740
He's around somewhere.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:53.000
He is, maybe.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:53.900
Thank you.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.390
Let's go out later.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.370
Come on, I'll get the boys.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:04.080
I'd rather you didn't say anything to anybody until I tell my brother.

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:10.190
I'm telling him in the morning at breakfast.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.460
Susie, don't you want me to be with you when you tell him?

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:20.950
Oh, Steve, your brother isn't as bad as he's painted. He's not perfect.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:24.330
But he isn't gonna like this, and he makes you nervous, not me.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.970
No, I take that back. He makes me nervous, too.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.910
Oh, Steve, let's don't talk about my brother.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:32.060
I missed you the last few days.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:34.530
I'll see you for you.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.990
Dedicate the next number to you and the next...

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.320
Monday, I'll stroke your light brown hair.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.920
And on Tuesday, Hassan Feather?

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:55.260
I realize I love...

00:11:58.640 --> 00:11:59.980
Meaning that Chinese...

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.680
Hi. Can more than two enjoy this?

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.120
Where'd those glossy prints you promised me?

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.660
You know, I can't place them later than the night.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.960
Thanks very much, just the same. Let's forget about it, huh?

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:15.560
Come on, Susie, it's cold out here.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:20.640
Let me apologize for getting you a press spread.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.600
It's been an honor serving you gratis.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:26.230
You know, Falco, I get the feeling you're always snooping around.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:28.570
Boys, what are you fighting about?

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:29.890
Kill me! Push me through!

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.820
and I walked into this hallowed ground without knocking.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:36.140
You know, I feel too good to fight with you,

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:37.200
but that isn't what I said.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:38.660
I said you're Snoop.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.700
Example A, what were you doing around my hotel the other night?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.140
I beg your pardon, I haven't been in a Bowery in years.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.140
Come on, boys, break it up.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:46.980
Look, the next time you want any information,

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.540
don't scratch for it like a dog.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.160
Just ask for it like a man.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.940
Boom, Susie, I'll drop you off.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.130
Steve, where's the hair again?

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:06.640
In a minute, Chico.

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:07.240
Okay.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.530
It's all the excitement.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:17.060
I'll go home and go to bed early, and you go to work.

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:20.290
Okay, just don't leave me in a minor key.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.440
Don't tell me you've been playing around with Leo Bartha.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:29.980
No, that's what I mean.

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.540
I'm being fired for what I didn't do.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:35.920
He came in last week on a real dull, rainy night.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.140
I knew he was, but I didn't let on.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.900
He kept staring at me all night. Are you listening?

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:43.750
Avidly, avidly. Um, he was staring.

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:47.860
Staring. Consequently, when he approached me on his way out, I wasn't surprised.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.180
He was doing a special Sunday piece on...

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.160
Cigarettes. And naturally...

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.080
You were thrilled about being interviewed.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.230
And, uh, were you interviewed?

00:13:58.180 --> 00:13:58.940
In his apartment.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:01.630
Where was his wife?

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.060
I don't know. It's a big apartment.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.740
Only I was an interviewer.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:09.860
In fact, I was totally unprepared for what happened.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.800
Oh, come on, Chickie. We're friends from way back.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.900
A big columnist comes into this club without his ball and chain,

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:18.640
and you make like a delicatess encounter.

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.000
What did you expect he was gonna do in his apartment?

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:24.730
But Sidney, sweetheart, man must have been out of his mind.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.170
It was only 11 o'clock in the morning.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:29.970
I was so taken aback, I said...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:36.160
anything that popped into my sleepy head i'm not mistaken i think i even ordered the man out of

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:42.460
his own house he was furious and by the time i could have been put in a tropical island mood i

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:48.360
was out on the street that night van cleef calls me into his office he's got nothing against me he

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:53.980
says only can't afford to antagonize columns so i tell him how i still have stony at the military

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:59.360
academy sydney you think you could do something uh that's what i'm thinking rita maybe

00:14:59.360 --> 00:14:59.900
See?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.380
Do you still keep your key under the mat?

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:06.050
You there at 2.30?

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:32.470
You're touchy, Sidney. Don't be so touchy.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:36.200
Do a guy a favor. Well, live and learn.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:39.270
You want a bite? You want something to eat?

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:40.390
No, no.

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:59.060
I wish you and Steve could like each other.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.060
We, uh, we stick in each other's craw.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:04.280
Yes, but why?

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:08.810
For one thing, he thinks J.J. is some kind of a monster.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:11.010
Don't you?

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:15.280
Susie, J.J. happens to be one of my very best friends.

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:19.120
I know, but someday I'd like to look into your clever little mind

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.700
and see what you really think of him.

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:22.980
Why do you come off making a remark like that?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.620
Who could love a man who makes you jump through burning hoops

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.200
like a trained poodle?

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.450
Do you think JJ really likes Steve?

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.620
Frankly, yes, much to my surprise.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.700
He thinks he's a big talent, and those boys will go a big mile, he thinks.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:51.160
You feel pretty strong about Dallas, don't you?

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:52.600
Yes.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:54.550
Wedding bells?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:56.970
I'm discussing it with JJ in the morning.

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.880
It makes me feel good to know that some people want me for myself,

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.780
not just because I'm our brother's sister.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.080
Come on, Chickie, I'm just gonna have to laugh at that.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:10.910
An attractive girl like you.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:17.120
I hope J.J. likes Steve, that he isn't just putting on an act.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:18.890
Why should he put on an act for him?

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:21.940
Chickie, he's told presidents where to go and what to do.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:29.970
The act would be for...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.920
For my sake, not for Steve's.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:39.830
For me, I'll be back in a minute.

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:43.700
Susie!

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.560
Susie, don't sell your brother short.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.320
Talk this over with him.

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:56.110
You'll find them a real friend.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.020
In case I see J.J. any message.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:10.360
Tell him for me that Steve is the first real man I've ever been in love with.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:58.200
coincidence i was just on my way coincidence running into the very man you've been ducking

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.900
all week this is my breast

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.840
You know, I tried to call you twice, but you're lying.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.360
Now, what do you do for that hundred a week?

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:05.610
Fall out of bed?

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:07.870
Jimmy, I was just on my way inside a job to hunt the guy.

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:08.450
I got a great...

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.370
We'll have this kid arrested for larceny.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:12.890
Listen, when the band was at Roseland, I was the one that...

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:13.790
That was two months ago.

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:15.870
Take your hands out of my pocket, thief.

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.590
Jimmy, now take it easy, Jimmy.

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:20.610
Why? It's a dirty job, but I pay clean money for it.

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:21.510
No more, you don't.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.250
What is this? Showing off for the girl they're supposed to hee in Korea?

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:26.650
He's clever. He knows where he's being fired.

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:29.270
If you're funny, James, I'm a pretzel.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:29.900
Drop.

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:35.110
Good night, Mr. Falco.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:35.990
I'm fine. Is he here?

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:37.460
Of course.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:38.340
Alone is around.

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:42.380
A son of her, an agent, and a thing with blonde, wavy hair.

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:48.300
Good evening.

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:53.990
Let me get to Mr. Hudson.

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:54.570
Yes, sir.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.310
He's right inside, Mr. Falco.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:57.250
So it isn't long distance.

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:03.440
J.J., it's Sidney. Could you come out for a minute?

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:13.530
I have to talk to you, J.J., that's why. Come in for a minute.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:27.840
Just a moment. I'm ringing. He doesn't answer. Shall I take a message?

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:29.520
Yes, I have.

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:34.580
Oh, uh, Sidney. Later.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:51.400
I'll be off and wish you were deaf and wore a hearing aid.

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:55.490
A simple flick of the switch, I could shut out the greedy murmur of little men.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:57.740
Judge, I need you in for two minutes.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.970
Mac. Yes? I don't want this man at my table.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:07.970
Forgive me, Harvey. We were interrupted.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:10.590
The Supreme Court story I was telling you, Justice Black.

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:12.200
Oh, yes, Justice Black, that's right.

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:14.470
I believe I had it in my column.

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:16.050
Last July, the lead item.

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:18.640
I believe that's precisely where I read it, too.

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.740
You see, J.J., where I get my reputation

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:22.800
for being the best-informed man in Washington.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.400
Now, don't kid a kidder.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:28.500
Well, I don't think we caught your name, young man.

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:29.980
Sidney Falco, sir, but...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.980
Everybody knows and admires you, Senator Walker.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.440
Every six years, I've become less convinced of that.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:39.100
This young lady is Miss Linda James.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:41.520
She's managed by Manny Davis.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.080
I know Manny Davis.

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:48.490
Everyone knows Manny Davis, except Mrs. Manny Davis.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:50.870
All right, Billy, shoot.

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:55.720
Sports cars are getting smaller and smaller in California.

00:21:57.360 --> 00:21:59.860
The other day, you were crossing Hollywood Boulevard, and you got hit by one.

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:02.670
And you had to go to the hospital to get it removed.

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:08.230
Lee, you're not following the column. I had it last week.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:13.620
Do you believe in capital punishment?

00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:14.570
Why?

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:16.920
A man has just been sentenced to death.

00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:28.980
Let me tell me, what exactly are the unseen gifts of this lovely young thing that you manage?

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:35.370
Well, she sings a little. You know, she sings and...

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:38.590
Man, his faith in me is simply awe-inspiring, Mr. Hunsaker.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:40.540
Actually, I'm still studying.

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:41.400
What subject?

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:45.280
Singing, of course. Straight concert and...

00:22:45.280 --> 00:22:48.700
Why, of course. You might, for instance, be studying politics.

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:51.100
Uh, me?

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:52.500
Why, the C.J.J. She's...

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:56.940
I mean, I... You must be kidding, Mr. Hunsaker. Me with my Jersey City brains.

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:58.900
Brains may be Jersey City.

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:08.540
clothes are training the rail are you an actor mr falco that's what i was thinking are you mr

00:23:08.540 --> 00:23:16.940
falco well how did you guess it miss jay he's so pretty that's how falco let it be said at once

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:23.800
there's a man of forty faces not one none too pretty and all deceptive you see that grin

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:29.970
that's the uh that's the charming street urchin face it's part of

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:32.500
He throws himself upon your mercy.

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:34.830
He's got a half dozen faces for the ladies.

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:37.190
But the one I like, the really cute one,

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:39.600
is the quick, dependable chap.

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:41.740
Nothing he won't do for you in a pitch.

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:43.110
So he says.

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:47.530
Mr. Falco, whom I did not invite to sit at this table tonight,

00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:49.210
is a hungry press agent

00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:53.060
and fully up to all the tricks of his very slimy trade.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:55.360
Match me, Sidney.

00:23:57.860 --> 00:23:58.880
Right this minute, J.J.

00:24:04.410 --> 00:24:06.890
I know, that Wonder Boy of yours opens at the Latin Quarter next week.

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:07.670
J.J., uh...

00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:08.410
Say goodbye, Lester.

00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:16.380
May I ask you a naive question, Mr. Falco?

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:19.510
Exactly how does a press agent work?

00:24:21.850 --> 00:24:25.480
Uh, answer the man, Sidney. He's trying to take you off the hook.

00:24:27.030 --> 00:24:28.530
You just saw a good example of it, Senator.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.180
The press agent eats a columnist's dirt and is expected to call it manna.

00:24:33.770 --> 00:24:36.830
But don't you help columnists by furnishing them with items?

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:42.800
Sure. A columnist can't do without us, except our good and great friend JJ forgets to mention that.

00:24:42.920 --> 00:24:45.220
You see, we furnish them with items.

00:24:45.340 --> 00:24:46.720
What, some cheap, gruesome gags?

00:24:46.740 --> 00:24:47.420
You print them, don't you?

00:24:48.090 --> 00:24:49.990
Yes, with your client's names attached.

00:24:50.510 --> 00:24:54.230
That's the only reason the poor slobs pay you to see their names in my column all over the world.

00:24:54.900 --> 00:24:56.760
Now I make it out you're doing me a favor?

00:24:56.840 --> 00:24:57.260
I didn't say that.

00:24:57.260 --> 00:24:59.980
The day I can't get along without a press agent's handout...

00:25:00.250 --> 00:25:02.810
I'll close up shop and move to Alaska lock, stock, and barrel.

00:25:03.810 --> 00:25:05.490
Sweep out my igloo. Here I come.

00:25:05.770 --> 00:25:08.530
Look, Manny, you wrote in here on the senator's shirt tail, so shut your mouth.

00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:11.610
Now come, J.J. That's a little too harsh.

00:25:12.190 --> 00:25:13.610
Anyone seems fair game for you tonight?

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:19.890
This man is not for you, Harvey, and you shouldn't be seen in public with him

00:25:20.460 --> 00:25:22.320
because that's another part of a press agent's life.

00:25:23.120 --> 00:25:25.180
They dig up scandal about prominent people

00:25:25.180 --> 00:25:27.800
and shovel it thin among colonists who give them space.

00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:29.960
There seems to be some illusion here that a scandal...

00:25:32.360 --> 00:25:33.140
We're friends, Harvey.

00:25:34.430 --> 00:25:37.370
We go as far back as when you were a fresh-kid congressman, don't we?

00:25:38.050 --> 00:25:40.410
Why is it that everything you say sounds like a threat?

00:25:41.350 --> 00:25:43.370
Maybe it's a mannerism, because I don't threaten friends.

00:25:44.380 --> 00:25:45.900
But why furnish your enemies with ammunition?

00:25:47.260 --> 00:25:50.320
You're a family man, Harvey, and someday, God willing, you may want to be president.

00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:55.040
And here you are, out in the open, where any hep person knows

00:25:55.040 --> 00:25:59.560
that this one is toting that one around for you.

00:26:04.380 --> 00:26:05.200
Are we kids or what?

00:26:07.440 --> 00:26:09.640
Next time you come up, you might join me on my TV show.

00:26:10.580 --> 00:26:13.190
Thanks, J.J., for what I consider sound advice.

00:26:14.500 --> 00:26:15.600
You'll thou and sin no more.

00:26:17.870 --> 00:26:18.190
Senator?

00:26:18.720 --> 00:26:19.460
No, Mr. Falco.

00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:24.820
The senator pay that check.

00:26:25.060 --> 00:26:26.260
I'll take care of it, Mr. Hatziker.

00:26:28.640 --> 00:26:28.940
President.

00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:29.800
Hello, J.J.

00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:33.420
A big toe would make a better president.

00:26:33.580 --> 00:26:34.560
Mr. Hunsaker's coming, Joe.

00:26:34.700 --> 00:26:35.420
Pick me a good one, Joe.

00:26:41.290 --> 00:26:41.590
Sal?

00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:47.520
Call's Dan. I'll be at El Morocco.

00:26:47.840 --> 00:26:48.500
Very good, Mr. Hunsaker.

00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:50.000
Where's your coat, Sidney? Saving tips?

00:26:51.820 --> 00:26:54.780
My curiosity's killing me, but what are you so rambunctious about tonight?

00:26:56.660 --> 00:26:57.660
There's your fat friend.

00:27:02.140 --> 00:27:16.140
How are you?

00:27:16.540 --> 00:27:19.840
Italian, Sidney. That shows Lieutenant Kellogg likes your people.

00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:23.000
It's my Brooklyn background, J.J. Good with Yiddies, too.

00:27:23.780 --> 00:27:25.860
Harry. Am I supposed to say uncle?

00:27:27.500 --> 00:27:28.640
Hello, Phil. How's the kids?

00:27:28.900 --> 00:27:29.980
Just great, Mr. Huntson.

00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:32.780
Anything fit for me to print tonight?

00:27:33.470 --> 00:27:35.150
Nah, just check downtown.

00:27:37.220 --> 00:27:39.950
What happened to that doll? The item you gave me last night, she's still alive?

00:27:40.070 --> 00:27:43.370
Yeah, in Bellevue. She's hanging on, but we still don't know if she was pushed.

00:27:43.550 --> 00:27:44.850
Maybe she jumped. Love suicide.

00:27:45.090 --> 00:27:45.690
Could be.

00:27:45.810 --> 00:27:47.760
Check that, will you, Phil? It's a real heartthrob.

00:27:49.430 --> 00:27:50.910
Harry, say hello to Sidney Falco.

00:27:51.910 --> 00:27:53.510
Tickle him a little, he's been a bad boy tonight.

00:27:53.890 --> 00:27:55.590
He called you my fat friend.

00:27:56.790 --> 00:27:58.160
I don't believe it.

00:27:58.880 --> 00:27:59.980
I know, I know the story.

00:28:02.160 --> 00:28:05.940
I call him the boy with the ice cream face.

00:28:06.300 --> 00:28:08.380
That's good. It's nice. In fact, it's apt, Harry.

00:28:09.010 --> 00:28:10.830
Yeah, I got eyes. I put things together.

00:28:11.970 --> 00:28:14.450
I remember once when you didn't quite put things together.

00:28:14.610 --> 00:28:16.860
I was the mayor man.

00:28:21.670 --> 00:28:23.490
I didn't mean to hit the boy so hard.

00:28:24.330 --> 00:28:26.170
That's when a fella really needed a friend.

00:28:26.370 --> 00:28:28.130
And I won't forget his initials, J.J.

00:28:28.350 --> 00:28:28.930
Mr. Hotziker.

00:28:30.220 --> 00:28:31.620
She died 20 minutes ago.

00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:32.820
That's your business.

00:28:33.020 --> 00:28:33.420
Thanks, Phil.

00:28:34.590 --> 00:28:35.030
See you, Harry.

00:28:38.250 --> 00:28:39.410
See you, Kello.

00:28:44.890 --> 00:28:47.130
Spanish that shows he likes to speak stew, huh?

00:28:48.830 --> 00:28:50.830
I like Harry, but I can't deny he sweats a little.

00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:53.500
Try to come back or I'll throw you out again.

00:28:53.680 --> 00:28:54.320
Just a minute.

00:28:54.480 --> 00:28:55.940
My heart's in here and I'll pay you.

00:28:55.940 --> 00:28:56.560
Leave him alone.

00:28:56.980 --> 00:28:57.580
Leave him alone.

00:29:01.630 --> 00:29:03.050
I love this dirty town.

00:29:11.780 --> 00:29:15.670
Sidney, conjugate me a verb, for instance, to promise.

00:29:17.840 --> 00:29:19.160
Promise to break up that romance.

00:29:19.540 --> 00:29:19.740
When?

00:29:20.280 --> 00:29:23.140
You want something done, JJ, but I doubt if you yourself know what's involved.

00:29:23.220 --> 00:29:24.860
I'm a schoolboy. Teach me, teach me.

00:29:24.900 --> 00:29:25.800
Why don't you break it up yourself?

00:29:25.940 --> 00:29:27.400
You know you could do it in a couple minutes flat.

00:29:27.680 --> 00:29:29.180
At this late date, you need explanations?

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:39.240
Susie's all I've got. Now she's growing up, I want my relationship with her to remain at least at par.

00:29:40.020 --> 00:29:42.900
I don't intend to do anything to antagonize her if I don't have to.

00:29:44.150 --> 00:29:45.710
Be warned, son. I'll have to blitz you.

00:29:47.100 --> 00:29:49.860
Frankly, J.J., I don't think you've got the cards to blitz me.

00:29:49.960 --> 00:29:50.340
I don't?

00:29:50.680 --> 00:29:52.340
Correct me if I'm wrong, but I don't think so.

00:29:52.560 --> 00:29:53.720
I'll listen for one more minute.

00:29:55.270 --> 00:29:57.030
About a year ago, I did you a certain favor.

00:29:57.700 --> 00:29:58.320
It was a thing?

00:29:58.600 --> 00:29:59.880
Well, I never did such a dirty thing.

00:30:00.580 --> 00:30:02.300
All right, all right. It's forgotten. Forget it.

00:30:02.540 --> 00:30:04.100
Which brings us up to five weeks ago.

00:30:04.570 --> 00:30:06.390
Sidney, I got a nasty little problem here.

00:30:06.610 --> 00:30:09.710
Do so and so and I'll appreciate it. Did I say no? Was I fussy?

00:30:09.890 --> 00:30:12.050
Look, I'm the first to admit it didn't yell as fast as we'd like.

00:30:12.270 --> 00:30:14.630
But why, all of a sudden, can't I get you on the phone?

00:30:15.030 --> 00:30:17.430
And why, as of this date, am I frozen out of the column?

00:30:17.470 --> 00:30:17.830
You finished?

00:30:18.030 --> 00:30:20.430
No, let me finish, J.J. I don't like this job.

00:30:20.760 --> 00:30:23.640
That boy is dumb on matinee days only. Otherwise, he's got a head.

00:30:23.850 --> 00:30:25.970
And Susan, like you said, is growing up two heads.

00:30:26.190 --> 00:30:28.530
What I mean, we got a slippery, dangerous problem here.

00:30:28.610 --> 00:30:29.760
Not we, Sidney. You.

00:30:30.090 --> 00:30:32.010
Correct me if I'm wrong, J.J., weep.

00:30:32.460 --> 00:30:35.140
Because if I'm gonna go out on a limb for you, you gotta know what's involved.

00:30:36.840 --> 00:30:39.160
My right hand hasn't seen my left hand in 30 years.

00:30:39.300 --> 00:30:40.680
I'll do it, J.J., don't get me wrong.

00:30:40.820 --> 00:30:42.900
In for a penny, in for a pound, I'll go through with it.

00:30:43.360 --> 00:30:45.720
But stop beating me on the head. Let me make a living.

00:30:46.150 --> 00:30:49.130
Sidney, what you promised, do it. Don't finagle around.

00:30:49.610 --> 00:30:50.650
It's later than you think.

00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:54.880
Excuse me, J.J., it's later than you think. That boy proposed to her.

00:31:02.270 --> 00:31:03.170
Susie told you that?

00:31:06.970 --> 00:31:08.050
What was her answer?

00:31:08.510 --> 00:31:10.050
She'll discuss it with you at breakfast.

00:31:12.800 --> 00:31:13.700
Means you've got a plan.

00:31:15.320 --> 00:31:15.800
Can you deliver?

00:31:16.310 --> 00:31:19.160
Tonight, before you go to bed.

00:31:20.070 --> 00:31:21.550
Cats in a bag and a bag's in a river.

00:31:22.280 --> 00:31:23.780
Don't be a two-time loser, Sidney.

00:31:24.560 --> 00:31:25.700
The penalty could be severe.

00:31:57.850 --> 00:31:59.230
Yeah, he's around here some point.

00:32:00.340 --> 00:32:01.620
Hi, Sid. Do you want a table?

00:32:01.760 --> 00:32:03.200
No, just hopping. Leo Botha been in?

00:32:03.440 --> 00:32:06.460
Hey, he's having supper with the missus. She's over there, and he's, uh...

00:32:12.370 --> 00:32:15.090
Hello, Leo. How goes the Sunday piece on cigarette girls?

00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:18.460
What told you about her?

00:32:19.560 --> 00:32:20.870
A cigarette girl? Rita.

00:32:21.390 --> 00:32:23.210
And she took out all her hairpins, too.

00:32:28.050 --> 00:32:29.870
I never had the pleasure of meeting your wife.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:30.820
Do you know what I wonder, Leo?

00:32:32.320 --> 00:32:34.940
I wonder maybe you can use a hot little item for tomorrow's column.

00:32:35.140 --> 00:32:36.200
What is this, black man?

00:32:51.650 --> 00:32:53.490
Leo, I've never had the pleasure of meeting your wife.

00:32:56.090 --> 00:32:56.950
Hey, Falco, Loretta.

00:32:57.720 --> 00:32:58.840
How do you do, Mr. Falco?

00:32:58.940 --> 00:32:59.360
How do you do?

00:32:59.610 --> 00:32:59.970
You know what?

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:01.220
I don't know anything about the horses. Sit down.

00:33:01.910 --> 00:33:04.250
Help yourself to a glass of this New York State champagne.

00:33:04.670 --> 00:33:06.130
That's what my husband buys me.

00:33:06.530 --> 00:33:08.650
These imported wines aren't what they're cracked up to be.

00:33:09.160 --> 00:33:11.000
Whose side are you on, Mr. Falco? His am I?

00:33:11.180 --> 00:33:13.520
Frankly, I'm a neutral observer for the United Nations.

00:33:14.020 --> 00:33:15.310
What's your first name?

00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:16.160
Sidney.

00:33:16.700 --> 00:33:18.460
Is the horse running tomorrow by that name?

00:33:18.800 --> 00:33:20.940
Why don't you stop this business with the $2 bets?

00:33:22.630 --> 00:33:25.150
Compensation, Leo, for the marginal life we lead.

00:33:26.600 --> 00:33:28.740
Sidney, did you hear the story about the cloak and suitor?

00:33:29.020 --> 00:33:29.700
Oh, that's right.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.820
I tell him, and I read it in Hunsaker's column first.

00:33:32.310 --> 00:33:33.850
Oh, you a spy for the other side?

00:33:34.270 --> 00:33:37.110
No. I actually sat down to give Leo an item.

00:33:37.940 --> 00:33:40.480
Leo, he wants to give you an item. Don't be selling.

00:33:41.720 --> 00:33:42.980
Would you mind your own business?

00:33:43.740 --> 00:33:44.140
Hitler.

00:33:46.750 --> 00:33:49.850
In case you want to use it, a line. No names mentioned.

00:33:50.920 --> 00:33:53.020
For your private information, the guy's name is Dallas.

00:33:55.220 --> 00:33:57.950
There's still a name here that gives off vibrations.

00:34:02.170 --> 00:34:04.250
Is there anything with a name like Cigarette Girl?

00:34:04.570 --> 00:34:07.540
Uh, Cigarette Girl. No.

00:34:08.140 --> 00:34:09.960
There's no name here like that.

00:34:11.520 --> 00:34:13.320
I don't print blind items.

00:34:13.540 --> 00:34:15.360
What is this? Chats or checkers?

00:34:16.130 --> 00:34:20.290
Neither does Hunsaker. He likes to use the real names.

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:26.540
Check.

00:34:27.550 --> 00:34:28.690
What am I missing here?

00:34:28.990 --> 00:34:29.970
This man is trying to hold...

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:37.520
a gun to my head that's the horse shotgun in the fifth you want to tell my wife something what

00:34:37.520 --> 00:34:42.400
what sidney was to tell you that you spilled champagne all go on i'm waiting tell her what

00:34:42.400 --> 00:34:46.600
are you getting excited about what are you nuts or something calm down sorry lori i can't let this

00:34:46.600 --> 00:34:54.700
man blackmail me blackmail wants me to print a dirty little smear item in exchange for keeping

00:34:54.700 --> 00:34:55.540
keeping his mouth shut.

00:34:56.430 --> 00:34:56.910
About what?

00:35:00.380 --> 00:35:03.840
Foolishly, Laurie, I hope you'll understand it.

00:35:05.460 --> 00:35:08.560
The cigarette girl, I was kidding around.

00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:09.920
With the girl, I mean.

00:35:11.360 --> 00:35:12.900
I was kidding. She took it seriously.

00:35:13.160 --> 00:35:18.700
It's a case of bad judgment, bad taste.

00:35:20.770 --> 00:35:21.790
Just sorry, that's all.

00:35:23.780 --> 00:35:28.550
Your friend Hunsick, tell him for me he's a disgrace to his profession.

00:35:30.090 --> 00:35:33.000
Never mind about my, my bilious private life.

00:35:33.710 --> 00:35:36.270
I run a decent, responsible column. That's the way it stays.

00:35:37.160 --> 00:35:38.300
Your man prints anything.

00:35:39.180 --> 00:35:41.700
Use any spice to pepper up his daily garbage.

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:43.240
You tell him I said so.

00:35:44.090 --> 00:35:47.380
Tell him that, like yourself, he's got the scruples of a guinea pig

00:35:47.380 --> 00:35:48.780
and the morals of a gangster.

00:35:48.960 --> 00:35:52.400
What do I do now? Whistle stars and stripes forever?

00:35:54.280 --> 00:35:56.640
What you do now, Mr. Falco, is crow like a hen.

00:35:57.810 --> 00:35:59.070
You have just laid an egg.

00:36:00.160 --> 00:36:04.690
Leo, this is the first clean thing I've seen you do in years.

00:36:28.060 --> 00:36:29.700
Mr. Elville wants to see you, Mr. Falcon.

00:36:41.480 --> 00:36:43.520
I see Bartha gave you a cold tongue for supper.

00:36:43.640 --> 00:36:46.880
