00:55:41.484 --> 00:55:41.864
See you.

00:55:42.636 --> 00:55:45.256
Don't be alarmed, but I want you to take a look at Elwell's column in the record.

00:55:46.124 --> 00:55:47.124
today.

00:55:48.012 --> 00:55:50.012
No, it's about me.

00:55:50.604 --> 00:55:51.184
A smear.

00:55:52.364 --> 00:55:53.204
A smear of a...

00:55:54.220 --> 00:55:55.180
What kind of a smear?

00:55:56.300 --> 00:55:58.360
We're on our way to the Elysian to dick her with Van Cleve.

00:55:58.736 --> 00:55:59.636
He's fired us already.

00:56:01.240 --> 00:56:02.720
Oh, look, I'll call you later, dear.

00:56:22.530 --> 00:56:25.610
I told Steve what I really think, he'd tear your head off.

00:56:26.480 --> 00:56:26.780
Tell him.

00:56:37.580 --> 00:56:38.140
What's the matter with you?

00:56:39.110 --> 00:56:39.450
Nothing.

00:56:46.630 --> 00:56:50.270
You know, Sally, I sometimes get the impression you think you live in Starbright Park.

00:56:50.600 --> 00:56:51.320
This is life.

00:56:51.460 --> 00:56:52.200
Get used to it.

00:57:11.040 --> 00:57:13.600
J.J., I presume you saw the Elwell smear.

00:57:15.190 --> 00:57:17.080
No, no, no metal. It's not yet.

00:57:18.100 --> 00:57:19.300
It's a lot worse than that.

00:57:20.600 --> 00:57:22.020
Auntie Van Cleave is firing him.

00:57:23.660 --> 00:57:25.220
I just got it from the horse's mouth.

00:57:25.640 --> 00:57:27.020
They were just here in a panic.

00:57:27.240 --> 00:57:29.290
You mean to say they've already traced the smear to you?

00:57:30.160 --> 00:57:31.180
Then what are you so smug about?

00:57:31.480 --> 00:57:32.200
Susie isn't dumb.

00:57:32.870 --> 00:57:34.410
All she has to do is put two and two together

00:57:34.410 --> 00:57:35.370
and I'm a chicken in a pot.

00:57:36.160 --> 00:57:38.540
J.J., peace on earth and goodwill to men.

00:57:38.720 --> 00:57:40.480
Everything's working out just the way I planned.

00:57:40.940 --> 00:57:42.960
I guarantee the bomb will pop right on schedule.

00:57:45.540 --> 00:57:46.360
Get him back his...

00:57:46.770 --> 00:57:48.520
You said get him back his job.

00:57:49.180 --> 00:57:49.600
For what?

00:57:49.860 --> 00:57:52.700
Look, Sidney, I don't like this.

00:57:52.760 --> 00:57:53.740
It's traveling in the dark.

00:57:54.170 --> 00:57:55.390
You better get over here as fast as you can.

00:57:56.440 --> 00:57:56.760
Now, wait a minute.

00:57:57.230 --> 00:57:57.930
Susie's up and about.

00:57:58.590 --> 00:57:59.970
We'll have to do a fine song and...

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.040
dance. Meet me at the TV about 3 o'clock.

00:58:34.540 --> 00:58:36.040
Susie, you're very much at my thoughts today.

00:58:37.560 --> 00:58:37.920
Why?

00:58:39.340 --> 00:58:39.580
Why?

00:58:41.310 --> 00:58:42.790
Questioned there with that newspaper in your hand.

00:58:48.820 --> 00:58:49.840
Didn't he tell you about it?

00:58:51.180 --> 00:58:51.900
Yes, he phoned.

00:58:53.810 --> 00:58:55.490
Susie, I don't know this boy too well.

00:58:57.520 --> 00:58:58.360
Anything in these charges?

00:59:00.960 --> 00:59:01.980
You're not being partial, are you?

00:59:02.620 --> 00:59:05.070
No, I'm not. I'm not.

00:59:05.230 --> 00:59:07.470
Now, take it easy, Susie. You don't have to protest with me.

00:59:08.180 --> 00:59:09.040
I'll trust your judgment.

00:59:09.300 --> 00:59:12.420
I'm in a camp, you poor kid. You look so nervous.

00:59:17.940 --> 00:59:18.500
Trembling, dear.

00:59:21.520 --> 00:59:23.480
Suddenly didn't take long to phone you, did he?

00:59:24.300 --> 00:59:29.540
Naturally. Anything that touches you touches me, doesn't it?

00:59:36.840 --> 00:59:38.480
You know, dear, we're drifting apart, you and I.

00:59:40.140 --> 00:59:40.940
And I don't like it.

00:59:42.780 --> 00:59:44.360
A year ago, in your wildest dreams,

00:59:44.540 --> 00:59:45.820
would you have walked past that door

00:59:45.820 --> 00:59:47.820
without coming in here to take up the situation with me?

00:59:48.100 --> 00:59:49.460
Today, I had to call you in.

00:59:49.870 --> 00:59:51.810
But I'm taking up the situation with you now.

00:59:52.050 --> 00:59:52.830
Let me finish, dear.

00:59:53.110 --> 00:59:54.590
You've had your say, let me have mine.

00:59:54.810 --> 00:59:56.490
But I haven't said anything, J.J.

01:00:02.270 --> 01:00:03.390
Susie, I want to help you.

01:00:06.130 --> 01:00:07.890
You're all I've got in this whole wide world.

01:00:09.100 --> 01:00:10.320
There's nothing I wouldn't do for you.

01:00:11.330 --> 01:00:12.530
What do you want me to do? Name it.

01:00:13.360 --> 01:00:15.020
Because I don't like that troubled look on your face.

01:00:17.810 --> 01:00:19.190
You really want to help me, J.J.

01:00:20.980 --> 01:00:22.360
Get Steve back his job.

01:00:23.830 --> 01:00:25.030
He means that much to you?

01:00:26.000 --> 01:00:26.320
Yes.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.280
It'll only take a minute.

01:00:32.070 --> 01:00:34.130
Ten cents worth of American tell and tell.

01:00:36.560 --> 01:00:37.460
You're picking up my lingo.

01:00:38.630 --> 01:00:40.110
I read your column every day.

01:00:47.160 --> 01:00:48.880
Susie, I like this crisp new attitude of yours.

01:00:49.640 --> 01:00:50.760
Growing up, and I like it.

01:00:51.560 --> 01:00:52.980
I don't like it when you're limp and dependent.

01:00:53.630 --> 01:00:54.550
When you're odd and wayward.

01:00:56.550 --> 01:00:57.650
This Dallas boy must be good for you.

01:00:59.160 --> 01:00:59.900
Why don't you bring him around today?

01:01:00.860 --> 01:01:02.940
This time, I'll clean my glasses for a better look.

01:01:03.720 --> 01:01:04.800
Let me have Billy Van Cleen.

01:01:04.900 --> 01:01:11.820
Never tell anyone, Susie, how I'm tied to your apron strings.

01:01:13.230 --> 01:01:14.860
Billy? J.J. Hunsaker.

01:01:16.300 --> 01:01:17.440
Now, what about this Dallas boy?

01:01:18.460 --> 01:01:20.100
That's right. What about this Dallas boy?

01:01:40.660 --> 01:01:43.630
The American way. Who said? The man said.

01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:46.500
Burton, don't hang around. If I run over, I'll cut some items off the tail.

01:01:47.580 --> 01:01:51.720
From Washington through Jefferson, from Lincoln and FDR, right up to today.

01:01:52.230 --> 01:01:54.870
The democratic way of life. That's what the man said.

01:01:55.420 --> 01:01:57.360
Nowadays, it doesn't export too well.

01:01:57.820 --> 01:01:59.980
You know and I know that our best secret weapon...

01:02:00.060 --> 01:02:03.640
is D-E-M-O-C-R-A-C-Y, democracy.

01:02:04.080 --> 01:02:04.600
That's grand.

01:02:04.840 --> 01:02:06.240
Let's never forget it, ladies and gentlemen.

01:02:06.560 --> 01:02:07.960
Just grand, J.J.

01:02:08.280 --> 01:02:09.460
Is my makeup all right?

01:02:09.720 --> 01:02:12.040
You know, despite the scouts and movies I've made, I'm...

01:02:12.040 --> 01:02:13.060
It's fine, it's fine. Mary, take care of Miss Tam.

01:02:13.180 --> 01:02:14.760
Anything she wants. She's our star today.

01:02:14.800 --> 01:02:15.920
I've never been a TV, thank you.

01:02:20.780 --> 01:02:24.680
That boy coming over here today.

01:02:25.290 --> 01:02:26.910
If I can trust my eyes, and I think I can,

01:02:27.030 --> 01:02:28.450
Susie knows all about your dirty work.

01:02:30.440 --> 01:02:34.520
I heard I had to get that boy's job back.

01:02:36.190 --> 01:02:40.360
Look, J.J., we can tie this off in a one neat bundle,

01:02:40.700 --> 01:02:42.500
address it to the dumps, to Oblivion.

01:02:43.100 --> 01:02:45.020
We're doing great, but please do it my way.

01:02:45.340 --> 01:02:47.800
I've cased this kid. I know his ins and outs.

01:02:48.350 --> 01:02:52.070
He's full of juice and vinegar just waiting for a big shot like you to put on the squeeze.

01:02:53.090 --> 01:02:54.750
You got the boy's job back, okay.

01:02:55.110 --> 01:02:58.750
But he's not gonna accept your favor. The manager, yeah, but not that boy.

01:03:03.230 --> 01:03:05.050
What has this boy got that Susie likes?

01:03:06.120 --> 01:03:08.370
Integrity. Acute. Like indigestion.

01:03:09.860 --> 01:03:11.910
What does this mean, integrity?

01:03:12.230 --> 01:03:13.830
A pocket full of firecrackers.

01:03:14.570 --> 01:03:19.980
Weight and patch. Oh, it's a new wrinkle.

01:03:20.400 --> 01:03:23.320
To tell you the truth, I never thought I'd make a killing on some guy's integrity.

01:03:26.410 --> 01:03:27.770
I'd hate to take a bite out of you.

01:03:28.550 --> 01:03:29.980
You're a cookie full of...

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:42.170
I still think he's responsible for the smears.

01:03:42.290 --> 01:03:44.870
Not that I'm convinced, but you'll never prove it in a thousand years.

01:03:45.870 --> 01:03:50.810
Steve, you'll do what you want, but it can't hurt.

01:03:51.360 --> 01:03:53.920
He offers you an olive branch, so today like dollars.

01:03:57.680 --> 01:03:58.080
Excuse me.

01:04:04.960 --> 01:04:07.480
Steve, before we go in, could I...

01:04:10.390 --> 01:04:13.750
All right, just in time. J.J. just finished up his rehearsal.

01:04:22.320 --> 01:04:23.200
