01:12:53.820 --> 01:12:55.560
Sidney, the syrup you're giving out with,

01:12:56.700 --> 01:12:58.800
you pour over waffles, not J.J. Hunsaker.

01:13:00.670 --> 01:13:02.830
What do you mean this lousy kid will give up my sister?

01:13:03.050 --> 01:13:07.760
How does it matter who's sister?

01:13:08.050 --> 01:13:09.390
The main thing is that they're true.

01:13:10.320 --> 01:13:11.100
I mean that...

01:13:11.100 --> 01:13:14.320
Am I supposed to forget how that kid talked to me today?

01:13:16.110 --> 01:13:19.130
J.J., is he worthy of a second glance from a man like you?

01:13:19.760 --> 01:13:20.540
I mean that...

01:13:20.540 --> 01:13:21.160
Fight on this.

01:13:21.340 --> 01:13:26.950
Team ship tickets.

01:13:27.280 --> 01:13:29.350
The next sailing with the Mary, as soon as he's run down.

01:13:32.560 --> 01:13:36.700
That louse is after Susie's hair for good.

01:13:36.920 --> 01:13:39.040
I want that boy taken apart.

01:13:46.360 --> 01:13:49.380
J.J., why do something that's gonna drive them

01:13:49.380 --> 01:13:50.900
right back into each other's arms?

01:13:51.040 --> 01:13:52.500
I know how to handle Susie. You just...

01:13:57.640 --> 01:13:58.480
Just handle the boy.

01:14:00.350 --> 01:14:01.130
Preferably tonight.

01:14:03.120 --> 01:14:04.220
What's tomorrow, a holiday?

01:14:09.660 --> 01:14:10.820
Fat cop, Fred.

01:14:12.990 --> 01:14:13.850
Think I'm going home.

01:14:14.700 --> 01:14:16.660
Maybe I left my sense of humor in my other suit.

01:14:16.760 --> 01:14:18.380
You've got a God-given brain, Sidney. Use it.

01:14:20.400 --> 01:14:21.580
This is a personal thing with me.

01:14:22.950 --> 01:14:25.450
Are you telling me I think of this in terms of personal pique?

01:14:26.630 --> 01:14:29.190
Don't you see that today that boy wiped his feet on the choice?

01:14:29.450 --> 01:14:29.970
On the pre-del...

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:33.040
of 60 million men and women in the greatest country in the world?

01:14:33.260 --> 01:14:38.260
If you had any morals yourself, you'd understand the immorality of that boy's stand today.

01:14:39.800 --> 01:14:42.760
It wasn't me he criticized. It's my readers.

01:14:49.170 --> 01:14:52.160
Gangplank, Sidney. You may want to get back on board.

01:14:54.000 --> 01:14:58.870
AJ, it's one thing to wear your door canoe and noose. I'd rather have my freedom.

01:14:59.210 --> 01:14:59.870
The man in jail...

01:15:02.370 --> 01:15:04.590
Except if you'll excuse me, J.J., I'm not in jail.

01:15:04.850 --> 01:15:07.740
You're in jail, Sidney. You're a prisoner of your own fears,

01:15:07.920 --> 01:15:09.560
your own greed and ambition. You're in jail.

01:15:09.680 --> 01:15:13.050
You're blind, Mr. Magoo. This is the crossroads for me.

01:15:13.420 --> 01:15:16.400
I won't get Kelo. Not for a lifetime pass to the Polar Grounds.

01:15:16.620 --> 01:15:18.840
Not if you served me Cleopatra on a plate.

01:15:19.140 --> 01:15:20.180
Sidney, I told you.

01:15:20.280 --> 01:15:23.660
J.J., I swear to you on my mother's life I wouldn't do that.

01:15:24.000 --> 01:15:26.320
Not if you gave me a column would I do a thing.

01:15:36.200 --> 01:15:39.620
Who do you suppose writes the column while Susie and I are away for three months?

01:15:40.820 --> 01:15:41.460
The man on the moon?

01:15:42.570 --> 01:15:43.310
Thank you, Sidney.

01:15:45.540 --> 01:15:47.020
Sidney, I'll have that piece of paperback.

01:15:47.180 --> 01:15:59.900
Two cups of coffee?

01:16:16.570 --> 01:16:19.820
I love the way you stood up to my brother.

01:16:22.370 --> 01:16:27.070
Nobody ever did that before, but it frightened me.

01:16:30.220 --> 01:16:31.180
Isn't that why you walked out?

01:16:34.090 --> 01:16:44.410
Yes, what you say to me, true, I'm weak, I can't change.

01:16:53.210 --> 01:16:55.960
Gather and say goodbye.

01:16:59.180 --> 01:16:59.420
Yes.

01:17:03.770 --> 01:17:06.470
I came here with half an idea of saying goodbye.

01:17:08.570 --> 01:17:09.610
I guess I'll hang around.

01:17:17.270 --> 01:17:18.710
Susie, is this really what you want?

01:17:24.350 --> 01:17:26.690
My brother's capable of doing you very great harm,

01:17:26.690 --> 01:17:28.270
and I can't let that happen. We can't...

01:17:28.270 --> 01:17:29.470
I won't give you up.

01:17:29.630 --> 01:17:29.970
We can't...

01:17:31.810 --> 01:17:34.490
Susie, that's fish four days old. I won't buy it.

01:17:35.920 --> 01:17:38.600
Right out of that mouth I love like a ventriloquist dummy,

01:17:38.740 --> 01:17:39.900
your brother is saying goodbye.

01:17:40.240 --> 01:17:45.650
No, Steve. Please don't. Please don't.

01:17:47.600 --> 01:17:51.700
At least this way I'll know that somewhere in the world,

01:17:51.760 --> 01:17:54.680
alive and happy, working...

01:17:57.170 --> 01:17:57.970
Won't give you up.

01:18:05.690 --> 01:18:06.550
You've got to go.

01:18:19.330 --> 01:18:20.310
Always hated this call.

01:18:39.370 --> 01:18:41.620
Bye, Mr. D'Angelo. Take care of Steve.

01:18:53.700 --> 01:18:55.440
Say something funny, Mr. Arson Pfeffer.

01:20:12.180 --> 01:20:16.380
Excuse me. Excuse me. Excuse me, Joe.

01:20:17.960 --> 01:20:19.420
Steve don't feel too good.

01:20:19.810 --> 01:20:20.930
Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

01:20:21.170 --> 01:20:23.750
So, if you don't mind, he'd like to leave after this set.

01:20:24.190 --> 01:20:27.990
I like that boy, Frank. Anything he wants to do is okay with me.

01:20:28.130 --> 01:20:28.410
Thanks.

01:20:36.360 --> 01:20:47.900
Hey, Mr. Falco, I hate to give you this satisfaction.

01:20:52.680 --> 01:20:54.220
Broke it off tonight for good.

01:20:55.000 --> 01:20:55.840
Tell that to Hunts.

01:20:56.800 --> 01:20:57.640
Tell him we agree.

01:20:57.880 --> 01:20:58.700
He's a big man.

01:20:58.860 --> 01:20:59.980
He wins all the marbles.

01:21:00.800 --> 01:21:00.920
Thank you.

01:21:38.090 --> 01:21:40.350
That's all the rush. I thought you said three o'clock.

01:21:42.470 --> 01:21:44.630
Sir, he's leaving early right after this set.

01:21:45.870 --> 01:21:48.150
It's nice, Sidney, you're giving me this tip.

01:21:48.560 --> 01:21:49.460
He's got him on him.

01:21:49.580 --> 01:21:50.720
And he's got him on him.

01:21:51.180 --> 01:21:52.940
I appreciate a thing like this.

01:21:53.600 --> 01:21:56.720
And I appreciate why you're looking out for the virtue of the city.

01:21:58.040 --> 01:21:59.160
Watch your hurry, sir.

01:21:59.200 --> 01:21:59.900
Let go of me, Kello.

01:22:00.280 --> 01:22:03.340
Hey, Murph, do you like this face?

01:22:04.160 --> 01:22:05.800
Well, I'll be doggone. It's melting.

01:22:06.280 --> 01:22:07.740
Something got you scared, Sidney?

01:22:09.040 --> 01:22:11.100
Listen, rectify me a certain thing.

01:22:11.780 --> 01:22:14.700
Weren't you kidding, Snooks, when you told J.J. I was fat?

01:22:17.910 --> 01:22:19.310
Just in peace, Kello, you're skinny.

01:22:20.500 --> 01:22:21.880
But J.J. says you're sweat.

01:22:24.920 --> 01:22:26.060
Is that a fact?

01:22:27.160 --> 01:22:28.460
He's a jelly, ain't he?

01:22:30.030 --> 01:22:33.430
I get the distinct impression, Snooks, that you don't like me.

01:22:34.160 --> 01:22:35.000
That I be wrong?

01:22:35.560 --> 01:22:37.480
You could be right, you fat slob.

01:22:40.020 --> 01:22:43.500
Come back, Sidney. I want to chastise you.

01:23:07.520 --> 01:23:07.800
Thank you very much.

01:24:08.960 --> 01:24:09.800
Hey, Bella.

01:24:30.350 --> 01:24:33.150
No, I told you I'm not taking any calls, right?

01:24:33.270 --> 01:24:35.530
I don't care who calls, no calls.

01:24:36.480 --> 01:24:37.860
I still want to make a toast.

01:24:38.140 --> 01:24:39.840
I'm buying a booze, so I'm making a toast.

01:24:39.960 --> 01:24:40.360
Okay!

01:24:41.020 --> 01:24:42.680
That's great for the thing we always dream about.

01:24:42.800 --> 01:24:43.960
It makes you cool in the summertime.

01:24:44.160 --> 01:24:45.360
It keeps you hot in the wintertime.

01:24:45.520 --> 01:24:46.180
It gets you good cooking.

01:24:46.220 --> 01:24:46.920
Hey, how you been?

01:24:47.040 --> 01:24:47.560
What do you say? Have a drink.

01:24:47.680 --> 01:24:48.080
Sidney.

01:24:48.440 --> 01:24:49.700
Hello, Charlie. How are you?

01:24:49.720 --> 01:24:50.840
I'm Herbie Temple, remember?

01:24:51.100 --> 01:24:52.300
Hey, listen, Sidney.

01:24:52.300 --> 01:24:53.520
I want to ask you something, Sidney.

01:24:53.540 --> 01:24:55.560
Gentlemen, I'm toasting my favorite new perfume.

01:24:57.530 --> 01:24:57.930
Success.

01:24:58.330 --> 01:24:59.390
Hey, boy.

01:25:01.980 --> 01:25:03.620
All right, kid, she said it was important.

01:25:03.800 --> 01:25:05.340
The operator at 21 took the message.

01:25:05.460 --> 01:25:08.320
Lou, I'm not taking any messages unless it's J.J. Hunsett.

01:25:08.360 --> 01:25:10.580
Well, that's who it is. He wants you to come over to his house right away.

01:25:10.720 --> 01:25:13.540
Gentlemen, duty calls, and the best of friends must part, right?

01:25:13.760 --> 01:25:14.560
All right, sit here.

01:25:14.980 --> 01:25:17.840
Al and I talked it over, and we want you to handle our economy.

01:25:18.140 --> 01:25:21.280
Uh, and what do you guys want to bread and butter a contract like I was looking for you?

01:25:21.540 --> 01:25:24.160
Hey, Sidney, why don't you take me low? Maybe I'll rub his back a little for you.

01:25:51.790 --> 01:25:52.030
Okay, Jay?

01:26:11.320 --> 01:26:11.600
JJ?

01:26:26.390 --> 01:26:26.850
Susie?

01:26:34.250 --> 01:26:47.940
Susie, what are you doing out there at this time of the night?

01:26:49.520 --> 01:26:53.580
The door was opened. Where's J.J.?

01:26:54.370 --> 01:26:55.110
He isn't here.

01:26:55.730 --> 01:26:57.130
I got a message to come over.

01:26:57.510 --> 01:26:57.850
Did you?

01:26:58.860 --> 01:26:59.980
Well, if he isn't.

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:00.400
You're right.

01:27:01.100 --> 01:27:02.280
Mr. D'Angelo phoned.

01:27:05.050 --> 01:27:05.350
Yeah?

01:27:06.320 --> 01:27:06.960
About Steve.

01:27:12.830 --> 01:27:16.050
I went down to the hospital, but they wouldn't let me in.

01:27:18.770 --> 01:27:20.150
It's all over town about Dallas.

01:27:22.140 --> 01:27:22.620
How is he?

01:27:27.000 --> 01:27:27.900
They wouldn't let me in.

01:27:30.760 --> 01:27:36.400
But I gave Steve up. Why didn't you and J.J. do it?

01:27:37.080 --> 01:27:40.880
What are you talking about? Who gives you the right to talk like that?

01:27:41.220 --> 01:27:45.770
Don't bother to lie, Sidney. I don't care anymore.

01:27:49.010 --> 01:27:51.050
Susie, you're very upset, so I'm not going to argue with you.

01:27:52.800 --> 01:27:54.540
Feeling sorry for yourself is not going to help.

01:27:55.040 --> 01:27:56.840
Why don't you go to bed and get a good night's sleep, huh?

01:27:57.800 --> 01:27:59.560
I'm sorry about Steve, not myself.

01:28:01.210 --> 01:28:02.410
I'm sorry about my brother.

01:28:05.150 --> 01:28:07.010
And I'm sorry about you, too, Sidney.

01:28:07.900 --> 01:28:09.160
Because you're going down with the ship.

01:28:09.360 --> 01:28:09.800
What ship?

01:28:10.200 --> 01:28:10.820
The ship.

01:28:14.290 --> 01:28:16.250
Don't you know how my brother's gonna see you after tonight?

01:28:18.040 --> 01:28:22.520
You're gonna be the man who drove his beloved little sister to suicide.

01:28:27.490 --> 01:28:29.430
You know, Susie, I've heard this woman talk before.

01:28:30.030 --> 01:28:31.590
Why don't you start growing up, huh?

01:28:33.500 --> 01:28:35.540
Start thinking with your head instead of your hips.

01:28:39.300 --> 01:28:42.850
Uh, by the way, I got nothing against women thinking with their hips.

01:28:43.320 --> 01:28:44.140
That's their nature.

01:28:45.090 --> 01:28:48.490
It's like it's a man's nature to go out and hustle and get the things he wants.

01:28:50.880 --> 01:28:52.000
Susie, look at yourself.

01:28:52.950 --> 01:28:56.470
You're 19 years old, just a kid, and you're falling apart at the seams.

01:28:57.150 --> 01:28:59.970
You're tiptoe around on those bird legs of yours, nervous.

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:06.320
and incompetent with a fatality for doing wrong picking wrong and giving up even before you start

01:29:06.320 --> 01:29:17.560
a fight minute the truth and the truth hurts come around some night when i'm not writing your

01:29:17.560 --> 01:29:24.090
brother's column and i'll revise that delicate outlook of life to give credit where credit is

01:29:24.090 --> 01:29:28.660
due susie that body of yours deserves a better fate than tumbling off some terrace

01:29:30.890 --> 01:29:34.690
Susie, a bed is the best friend a girl ever had.

01:29:35.810 --> 01:29:36.470
Pleasant dreams.

01:29:40.870 --> 01:29:41.910
Now, don't be no square.

01:29:42.250 --> 01:29:43.110
Don't do anything stupid.

01:29:51.070 --> 01:29:51.510
Susie.

01:30:01.530 --> 01:30:28.670
If I told him you tried a thing like that.

01:30:38.090 --> 01:30:42.560
Susie, look, I'm sorry if I said anything or did anything.

01:30:42.640 --> 01:30:43.280
Get out of here!

01:30:44.420 --> 01:30:54.720
It's all right, Susie, I'm here.

01:31:00.120 --> 01:31:00.760
Take it easy, dear.

01:31:03.670 --> 01:31:04.490
Jesus, it wasn't...

01:31:04.490 --> 01:31:05.690
Calm yourself, dear. Now, don't worry.

01:31:18.480 --> 01:31:19.000
It's on the system.

01:31:33.100 --> 01:31:35.380
JJ, it's lucky I came right over after I got your message.

01:31:35.600 --> 01:31:37.480
I got here as quickly as I could, but...

01:31:37.480 --> 01:31:42.890
What message? What message?

01:31:44.250 --> 01:31:46.670
Well, be that as it may, someone call me...

01:31:49.480 --> 01:31:51.820
It's just lucky I got your message and came over here in time.

01:31:52.080 --> 01:31:52.320
Why?

01:31:55.040 --> 01:31:57.780
JJ, Susie was so depressed she tried to kill herself.

01:31:58.560 --> 01:31:58.920
Depressed?

01:32:02.330 --> 01:32:02.790
About what?

01:32:03.870 --> 01:32:05.190
Well, she heard the news about Dallas.

01:32:10.570 --> 01:32:11.370
News about Dallas?

01:32:16.140 --> 01:32:19.970
Oh, uh, I took it for granted, J.J., that you heard about it around town.

01:32:20.740 --> 01:32:24.100
You're not gonna like this, but they, uh, they picked him up on a marijuana rap.

01:32:25.050 --> 01:32:27.110
And is that why you put your hands on my sister?

01:32:32.270 --> 01:32:32.850
JJ, please.

01:32:34.440 --> 01:32:36.340
Susie tried to throw herself off the territory.

01:32:39.450 --> 01:32:40.490
Susie, tell him the truth.

01:32:50.580 --> 01:32:50.860
Please.

01:32:51.120 --> 01:32:52.160
Look, I can explain.

01:32:54.890 --> 01:32:55.370
JJ!

01:33:00.540 --> 01:33:06.240
I can't do the fucking sister, you big phony!

01:33:06.460 --> 01:33:07.640
Didn't you tell me to get Kello?

01:33:08.020 --> 01:33:08.480
Didn't you...

01:33:08.480 --> 01:33:21.870
I know he's lying about your attempted suicide.

01:33:22.700 --> 01:33:23.800
You know he's lying about me.

01:33:25.740 --> 01:33:26.960
We can't leave it like this, can we?

01:33:31.560 --> 01:33:32.700
I suggest you go to bed, dear.

01:33:37.680 --> 01:33:38.500
You're growing up.

01:33:44.560 --> 01:33:46.020
Sergeant, J.J. Hunsman.

01:33:46.100 --> 01:33:47.720
Let me talk to Lieutenant Keller.

01:33:48.720 --> 01:33:49.140
Hello, Harry.

01:33:49.850 --> 01:33:51.950
Sorry to bother you, kid, but a bad mistake has been made.

01:33:52.070 --> 01:33:55.270
J.J., you've got such contempt for people, it makes you stupid.

01:33:55.700 --> 01:33:56.860
You didn't beat those kids.

01:33:57.240 --> 01:33:58.120
You've lost them.

01:33:58.810 --> 01:33:59.870
You'll never get her back.

01:34:00.250 --> 01:34:03.860
Harry, Sidney Falco planted that stuff on Dallas.

01:34:05.510 --> 01:34:09.740
Jealousy. Behind my back, he was trying to make my sister.

01:34:10.530 --> 01:34:13.960
Fat could break my bones, but he'll never stop me from telling what I know.

01:34:14.580 --> 01:34:29.580
He's leaving right now. You're going?

01:34:38.060 --> 01:34:39.540
I'm leaving. I'm going to Steve.

01:34:42.310 --> 01:34:45.420
No, you're not. You're going into the hands of a good psychoanalyst.

01:34:45.720 --> 01:34:46.920
You tried to kill yourself tonight.

01:34:51.740 --> 01:34:58.500
Yes. I'd rather be dead than living with you.

01:35:18.240 --> 01:35:19.560
all the things you've done, JJ.

01:35:20.370 --> 01:35:24.820
I know I should hate you, but I don't.

01:35:25.660 --> 01:35:26.200
Pity you.
